const TS=`___ in the Arctic, polar bears depend on sea ice to hunt seals.|Living|They live|Lived|To living|主語 polar bears と能動関係 → 現在分詞の分詞構文。
The first successful vaccine was developed by Edward Jenner, ___ worked as a country doctor.|who|which|he|whom|人・主格の非制限用法 → who。
Saturn is famous for its rings, ___ are made mostly of ice.|which|that|they|what|非制限用法 which。
Not until the 1800s ___ widely used as a fuel.|was coal|coal was|coal|did coal be|Not until 文頭 → 倒置（be 動詞）。
Hummingbirds are the only birds ___ can fly backward.|that|they|which they|what|主格の関係代名詞 that。
The longer a tea bag is left in water, ___ the tea becomes.|the stronger|stronger|the strongest|the more strong|the + 比較級構文。
The Wright brothers' first flight lasted ___ 12 seconds.|only|only of|alone|single|副詞 only + 数。
Rubber trees are native ___ South America.|to|of|in|from|be native to「～原産の」。
The violin, ___ four strings, is played with a bow.|which has|it has|has|having it|非制限用法 which has。
___ the invention of the refrigerator, people preserved food with salt and ice.|Before|Until when|Since|Prior|前置詞 Before + 名詞。
It was Marie Curie ___ first won two Nobel Prizes.|who|which|whom|whose|強調構文（人）は who / that。
The more trees are cut down, ___ animals lose their homes.|the more|more|the most|much more|the + 比較級構文。
The cello is larger than the violin but smaller ___ the double bass.|than|as|to|from|比較級 + than。
Not only ___ on land, but frogs also live in water.|do frogs live|frogs live|live frogs|frogs do live|Not only 文頭 → 倒置。
Amelia Earhart was the first woman ___ alone across the Atlantic.|to fly|flying|flew|flies|the first + 名詞 + to do。
Opossums pretend to be dead when ___ by predators.|threatened|threatening|they threaten|to threaten|when (they are) threatened。
___ rich in vitamins, carrots are good for the eyes.|Being|Been|They being|To being|分詞構文 Being。
The oldest known cave paintings are ___ 40,000 years old.|more than|more of|most than|over of|more than + 数。
Whether there is life on Mars ___ unknown.|remains|remain|remaining|to remain|名詞節（Whether ～）は単数扱い。
Rain forests receive ___ rainfall than any other land habitat.|more|most|much|many|比較級 + than any other。
Some dinosaurs were no bigger ___ chickens.|than|as|to|that|no + 比較級 + than。
___ hot or cold, the desert can be dangerous.|Whether|Either|If|Both|Whether A or B「AであろうとBであろうと」。
Coffee was so popular in 18th-century London ___ hundreds of coffeehouses opened.|that|as|which|than|so ～ that。
The Moon has ___ atmosphere to speak of.|no|not|none|nor|no + 名詞。
Benjamin Franklin is known ___ his experiments with electricity.|for|as|to|by|be known for「～で知られる」。
Most birds build nests, ___ some lay eggs directly on the ground.|but|so|or|for|逆接 but。
___ the 1920s, radio became a popular form of entertainment.|In|On|At|Since in|年代は in。
The cell membrane controls ___ enters and leaves the cell.|what|which|that|it|先行詞を含む what。
Hardly ___ the experiment begun when the equipment failed.|had|has|did|was|Hardly had S p.p. when ...。
Volcanic soil is often very fertile, ___ farmers to live near volcanoes.|leading|led|leads|to lead|結果を表す分詞構文。
The koala sleeps up to 20 hours a day ___ conserve energy.|to|for|so|by|目的の to 不定詞。
So successful ___ that it was translated into 50 languages.|was the book|the book was|did the book|the book|So + 形容詞が文頭 → 倒置。
The ancient Greeks believed that the Earth ___ the center of the universe.|was|is being|were|be|過去の信念 → 時制の一致で was。
___ water freezes, it expands.|When|What|Which|That|時の接続詞 When。
Glass, ___ is made mainly from sand, was first produced in ancient times.|which|that|it|what|非制限用法 which。
It is the Moon's gravity ___ causes most tides.|that|what|which it|it|強調構文 It is ～ that。`;
const TE=`{The} {Statue} of Liberty {was gave} to the United States {by} France.|3|受動態 → was given。
{A} {honey} bee can {visits} {hundreds} of flowers a day.|3|助動詞 can + 原形 → visit。
The {Sahara} is {the} {most large} desert {in} Africa.|3|large の最上級 → largest。
{Neither} of the two {plans} {were} {accepted}.|3|neither of ～ は単数扱いが原則 → was。
The {children} {was} {excited} {about} the trip.|2|主語 children は複数 → were。
{Mozart} {began} {composed} music at the age {of} five.|3|begin doing / to do → composing。
The {scientists} {conducted} {an} experiment {in} last year.|4|last year の前に前置詞は不要。
Bamboo {is} one of the {fast} growing {plants} {on} Earth.|2|最上級 → fastest。
Benjamin Franklin, {who} {was} a printer, {he} also {invented} the lightning rod.|3|主語の重複 → he を削除。
{Lions} {hunting} {mainly} at {night}.|2|動詞が必要 → hunt。
The {museum} {will} {opened} {next} month.|3|助動詞 + 原形 → open。
Antarctica is {colder} {than} {any} other {continents}.|4|any other + 単数 → continent。
{Before} {the} invention of the telephone, people {communicate} by {letter}.|3|過去のこと → communicated。
{Rice} {is} {grew} in many parts of {Asia}.|3|受動態 → grown。
Scientists {have} {studied} dolphins {for} {decade}.|4|複数 → decades。
{Owls} can {see} {good} {in} the dark.|3|動詞修飾 → well。
{It} was {so} a beautiful day {that} we went to the {beach}.|2|a + 形 + 名 → such。
{Many} people {believe} {what} exercise {improves} mood.|3|名詞節 → that。
{The} {informations} in the report {was} {accurate}.|2|information は不可算 → information。
Elephants {have} {a} excellent {memory} {for} faces.|2|母音で始まる excellent → an。
{During} {the} {Middle Ages}, most people {can not} read.|4|過去 → could not。
{The} desert {is} {extreme} hot during the {day}.|3|形容詞修飾 → extremely。
{Most} {of} the students {has} {finished}.|3|Most of the students（複数）→ have。
{A} {numbers} of birds {were} {flying} south.|2|a number of → number（単数形）。
Sharks {have} {existing} {for} {millions} of years.|2|have + 過去分詞 → existed。
{It} {is} {necessary} for students {reading} widely.|4|It is ～ for 人 to do → to read。
The {river} {is} {wide} {than} it looks.|3|比較級 → wider。
{Both} the teacher {and} the students {was} {surprised}.|3|both A and B は複数 → were。
{Plants} {need} {sunlight}, water, {or} nutrients to grow.|4|列挙 → and。
The book {that} I {borrowed} {it} from the library {was} interesting.|3|関係代名詞の目的語と重複 → it を削除。
{Galileo} {improved} the telescope {and} {discovering} Jupiter's moons.|4|並列 → discovered。
The {city} {is} {famous} {to} its beautiful parks.|4|be famous for。
{Most} {of} the {world's} water {are} salty.|4|most of + 不可算 → is。
The {tallest} building in the {city} {have} 80 {floors}.|3|主語 building は単数 → has。
The {professor} {asked} us {to} {writing} an essay.|4|to + 原形 → write。
Coffee {contains} caffeine, {who} {can} keep people {awake}.|2|物 → which。
The {temperature} {has} {raised} {steadily} this week.|3|自動詞 rise → risen。
{An} {university} {student} {was} interviewed.|1|university は子音 /j/ で始まる → A。`;
